ts. The Completion and Production Services segment offers a range of equipment and services that are used to establish and maintain the flow of oil and natural gas from a well throughout its life cycle. The Downhole Technologies segment provides oil and gas perforation systems, and downhole tools in support of completion, intervention, wireline, and well abandonment operations. This segment also designs, manufactures, and markets its consumable engineered products to oilfield service, and exploration and production companies. The Offshore Manufactured Products segment designs, manufactures, and markets capital equipment utilized on floating production systems, subsea pipeline infrastructure, and offshore drilling rigs and vessels. Its products include flexible bearings, advanced connector systems, high-pressure riser systems, managed pressure drilling systems, deepwater mooring systems, cranes, subsea pipeline products, and blow-out preventer stack integration products. This segment also provides short-cycle products; and other products for use in industrial, military, alternative energy, and other applications. In addition, it offers specialty welding, fabrication, cladding and machining, offshore installation, and inspection and repair services. The company serves various national oil and natural gas, major and independent oil and natural gas, offshore drilling and other oilfield service, and defense and industrial companies. The company was incorporated in 1995 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lloyd A. Hajdik CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $308K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers, with revenue falling 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $34K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Oil States International, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $513M market cap on $669M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and -5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $74M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -12.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.7pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 30% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(OIS) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/OIS_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_110726010602_1794031562.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794031562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Oil States International Inc (OIS) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Backlog and ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/oil-states-international-inc-ois-190150660.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793732510.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Oil States International (OIS) Stock Climbs On Q3 Results As Backlog Builds","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/oil-states-international-ois-stock-171015397.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793553015.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Oil States International (OIS) Stock Rallies As Q3 Results Sharpen Margin Questions","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-ois/oil-states-international/